  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Five different companies each sent three representatives to attend a conference, where they sat around a circular table. How many seating arrangements are there if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$14! = 87\\,178\\,291\\,200$",
          "worked": "There are $5\\times3=15$ distinct representatives around the circle.\n$$N = (15-1)! = 14! = 87\\,178\\,291\\,200.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "representatives from the same company all sit together?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4!\\times(3!)^5 = 186\\,624$\n\nArrange five company blocks around the circle, then arrange the three representatives inside each block.",
          "worked": "Treat each company's representatives as a block. The five blocks have $4!$ circular arrangements. Each block has $3!$ internal orders.\n$$N = 4!\\times(3!)^5 = 186\\,624.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q19-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "a particular company’s representatives all sit together, but the other four companies’ representatives are happy to sit anywhere?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3!\\times12! = 2\\,874\\,009\\,600$\n\nTreat the specified company's representatives as one block, with $3!$ internal orders.",
          "worked": "The specified company's three representatives form one block with $3!$ internal orders. The block and the other 12 representatives form 13 entities around the circle.\n$$N = 3!\\times(13-1)! = 3!\\times12! = 2\\,874\\,009\\,600.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q19-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "a particular company’s representatives decide not to sit adjacent to each other?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$11!\\times12\\times11\\times10 = 52\\,690\\,176\\,000$\n\nArrange the other 12 representatives around the circle, then place the three specified representatives in distinct gaps.",
          "worked": "Arrange the other 12 representatives around the circle in $11!$ ways. There are 12 gaps between consecutive representatives, including the gap across the circular join. Place the three specified representatives in distinct gaps, giving $12\\times11\\times10$ choices.\n$$N = 11!\\times12\\times11\\times10 = 52\\,690\\,176\\,000.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q19-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "representatives from each company sit together, and the five companies appear around the table in a specified clockwise order?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(3!)^5 = 7\\,776$\n\nThe circular order of the five blocks is fixed; only their internal orders vary.",
          "worked": "Treat each company as a block. The specified clockwise order gives one circular arrangement of the five blocks. Each block has $3!$ internal orders.\n$$N = (3!)^5 = 7\\,776.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
